# The two dated, append-only records take git's built-in union merge: when two branches both add an entry at the
# end, a merge keeps both sides' lines instead of stopping on a conflict. What it risks is in docs/build-notes.md
# ("Union merge for the two append-only records"): read the file again after any merge that touched one entry.
docs/decision-log.md merge=union
docs/build-notes.md merge=union

# `sssb remove-items` reads these two diffs line by line: a CRLF checkout would put a carriage return into every path
# and every line it compares, and refuse every file.
packages/tools/src/remove-items/*.patch text eol=lf
